Licence notice for furios_app
=============================

This repository contains only code of our own (MIT, see LICENSE):
misc-de.py, the app icon, the launcher entry, the installer and the tests.
Every one of those files carries an SPDX header saying so.

At runtime it uses:
  - GTK 4 and libadwaita (LGPL-2.1+), through PyGObject (LGPL-2.1+)
  - GLib and Gio (LGPL-2.1+), from the same source
  - icons from the Adwaita icon theme (CC-BY-SA 3.0 / LGPL-3):
      audio-speakers-symbolic, network-cellular-symbolic,
      find-location-symbolic, changes-prevent-symbolic,
      battery-good-charging-symbolic, software-update-available-symbolic

It calls, without shipping them:
  - git, sudo and pkexec (polkit)
  - audioctl, modemctl, gpsctl, killswitch-indicator and battctl - the five
    tools this app drives

Those tools live in repositories of their own and have licences of their
own. Anybody installing them through this app is not installing MIT code:
the package from furios_pipewire is LGPL-2.1 (it compiles Jolla code in),
the one from furios_modem_fixes is GPL-2.0 (it patches a GPL file of
ofono2mm). furios_gps, furios_killswitch and furios_misc are MIT
throughout. The details are in the NOTICE of the respective repository; the
overview is under "Licence" in the README.

The app icon de.misc-de.tools.svg is drawn by us.

No part of FuriOS is patched or replaced. The app changes nothing itself -
it calls the tools that do.
